   $q$The function $f(x) = 4x - 6$ is graphed only for $-1 \le x \le 3$. What is the range of this graph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$-10 \\le y \\le 6$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$2 \\le y \\le 18$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-intercept-instead-of-subtracting"},{"text":"$-2 \\le y \\le 6$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-evaluating-negative-input"},{"text":"$-1 \\le y \\le 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-domain-as-range"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-10 \le y \le 6$$q$, $q$The graph is a segment with endpoints at $x = -1$ and $x = 3$. $f(-1) = 4(-1) - 6 = -10$ and $f(3) = 4(3) - 6 = 6$. Since the line rises, the $y$-values run from $-10$ to $6$. The range $-2 \le y \le 6$ treats $4(-1)$ as $4$.$q$, 'draft', null)
