  ('df7435e0-c4ec-5b8f-84e7-f54b2b8e2164', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'graphing-linear-functions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A line passes through $(-3, 8)$ and $(6, 2)$. Where does it cross the $y$-axis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y = \\frac{7}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-slope"},{"text":"$y = 10$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-slope"},{"text":"$y = 9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-x-intercept"},{"text":"$y = 6$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y = 6$$q$, $q$The slope is $\frac{2 - 8}{6 - (-3)} = \frac{-6}{9} = -\frac{2}{3}$. Using $(-3, 8)$: $8 = -\frac{2}{3}(-3) + b = 2 + b$, so $b = 6$. The value $9$ is where the line crosses the $x$-axis, not the $y$-axis.$q$, 'draft', null)
